s many uses. One of them is to tie a thing to another thing. Thankfully Neckbeard is a sloppy captain.","isAppLine":false,"small":{"start":0.16,"end":8.768,"frac":1.0,"status":"ok","matched":21,"words":21},"large":{"start":0.16,"end":8.768,"frac":1.0,"status":"ok","matched":21,"words":21},"differ":false},{"i":1,"text":"You dive into the water, grab the rope, and loop it around one of the pier's columns, tie a quick knot, then surface, gasping. Treading water, you see the rope pull tight and the ship start to angle, the rope sweeping across the deck as she does. One by one Captain Neckbeard and what little crew he has are swept overboard.","isAppLine":false,"small":{"start":9.568,"end":27.68,"frac":1.0,"status":"ok","matched":61,"words":61},"large":{"start":9.568,"end":31.104,"frac":0.869,"status":"ok","matched":53,"words":61},"differ":true}],"unassigned":{"small":[{"start":27.78,"end":30.8,"words":9,"text":"quick what are you waiting for get on board"}],"large":[]},"image":"https://creator.storycity.app/media/69026d1b54455_PC%20JM13.png"}